:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>Changelog</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Updated Vanilla to v0.5.13.6</strong>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Added Perfumery</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Learn perfume-making through <strong>Poppy's four lessons</strong>, or buy a beginner's manual if Poppy is disabled.</li>
					<li>Extract aromas from flowers and food, choose which scent qualities to keep, and save extraction profiles.</li>
					<li>Compose <strong>three layer of notes</strong>, adjust spirit and strength, blend manually or quickly, then bottle and mature perfumes.</li>
					<li>Name your perfumes, generate different bottle appearances, and save formulas to recreate them later.</li>
					<li>Added Poppy's discoveries, gifts, collaborations, and a guided Opium session using the existing Opium effects.</li>
					<li>Added Avery's perfume commissions, negotiations, deliveries, and follow-up conversations with Poppy.</li>
					<li>Wear perfume from the cabinet, Journal, or POCKET. Scents change and fade over time, wash off, fade faster in rain, and can affect wildlife.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Water Dragon: The Warrior's Rite</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Added a late-game island quest for <strong>full Water Dragons</strong> who have completed the spear quest and returned to the island, either by swimming or with Zephyr.</li>
					<li>Find carved stones on the shore or in the woods, consult the Elder, and meet the old islander beneath the castle to translate their records.</li>
					<li>Follow clues to a hidden passage in the sheltered bay and complete the <strong>Current, Stone, and Echo</strong> trials.</li>
					<li>Repair the old sea gate, decide whether to share the discovery with the islanders, then return to the Elder.</li>
					<li>Optional final-chamber reward: with <strong>1,000 Swimming</strong> and <strong>Physique, Athletics, or Willpower at its normal maximum</strong>, gain one extra permanent <strong>Tempered</strong> talent without using a talent slot.</li>
					<li>Unlocks the <strong>Heir of the Tide</strong> feat. Quest progress is recorded in the Journal, and leaving the tunnels does not reset completed trials.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Reworked Horse Racing</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Races have fairer odds, more varied events, and rare serious injuries. Placing a bet no longer puts the chosen horse at risk.</li>
					<li>Added <strong>Place Bet</strong>: bet on a horse finishing first or second for a better chance to win but a smaller payout.</li>
					<li>Betting limits now cap payouts at <strong>£10,000 per slip</strong>. The bookie's suspicion can reduce winnings after race rigging.</li>
					<li>Rebalanced Four-leaf Clover and moor Luck bonuses.</li>
					<li>Race logs and results are clearer, and watching or skipping a race now produces the same outcome.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Expanded cane use for blindfolded players</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>An intact, equipped cane reduces blindness-related skill-check failure by <strong>20%</strong>.</li>
					<li>Relying on a cane slows Blindfold Adaptability training to <strong>one-quarter speed</strong>.</li>
					<li>Canes can be used and broken in combat like umbrellas. Breaking or losing one immediately removes the assistance.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Added new and restored scenes</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Deep forest: a tree with faces may try to grab you. Run, cower, or howl if your Wolf transformation allows it.</li>
					<li>Orphanage garden: join other orphans in hide-and-seek.</li>
					<li>Adult shop: speak to Sydney while they work at the counter.</li>
					<li>Café chef blackmail: remaining defiant on the drive may make the police decide you're too much trouble to sell.</li>
					<li>Serpent's Maze: pull away rotten gate boards for a shortcut; the right path now leads to an overgrown garden, reflected on the minimap.</li>
					<li>Livestock: refuse Harper's examination outright.</li>
					<li>Domus windows: someone behind the curtain may be awake.</li>
					<li>Restored interactions with the asylum staircase and livestock barn door.</li>
					<li>Fixed the maths-project drugged exit from Alex's cottage so it leads to the farm rather than a town alley.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Expanded sewing and clothing sales</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>The tailor now buys old clothes for <strong>20% of their base price</strong>.</li>
					<li>Once you own a sewing kit, discarding clothes from your wardrobe gives <strong>one spool per piece</strong>.</li>
					<li>After buying a sewing kit, the tailor offers the <strong>Sewinator-9000</strong> in your orphanage room.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Expanded Poppy scenes and X-Change interactions</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Poppy can now receive X-Change pills during sex, with dialogue when shown a pill and after its effects take hold.</li>
					<li>Added dialogue for virginity, pill/body reveals, condoms, leg locks, scratching, requests, chastity, oral, penetration, climax, and other interactions.</li>
					<li>Fixed Poppy's final idle line never appearing.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Added Insanity reactions to intimidation</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Players with permanent or acquired Insanity may laugh hysterically or taunt attackers in selected scenes.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Expanded Robin's café-renovation interactions</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Robin now stays home while café shifts are cancelled for renovations and still runs the beach drinks stand during normal weekend hours.</li>
					<li>Added a conversation about the expansion, with responses depending on Robin's Confidence.</li>
					<li>Wages and job dialogue now reflect the closure correctly.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Added Android APK save recovery backups</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Updated APKs keep <strong>three recent recovery copies</strong> that can be restored from the Saves screen if normal save slots disappear.</li>
					<li>Improved save-loss warnings, storage diagnostics, and recovery handling.</li>
					<li><strong>Important:</strong> uninstalling the APK or clearing its app data also deletes these recovery copies. Exported backups are still necessary.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Colosseum post-win scenes are now optional</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Winners can take <strong>half the purse and ranking points</strong> without taking a pill or continuing the breeding aftermath.</li>
					<li>Added a visible <strong>Stop</strong> option without a permanent ban for ending early.</li>
					<li>Clarified choices and early-exit narration, and fixed an old-save issue affecting unrelated NPC pregnancy records.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Rebalanced next-day cramps</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Increased the daily orgasm threshold before cramps occur and made Sex skills improve tolerance.</li>
					<li>Reduced excessive tiredness and stopped denied climaxes from counting towards next-day soreness.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Improved Gender Identity and pronoun tolerance</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Rejected neutral traits no longer hold back Gender Identity changes or slow physical changes.</li>
					<li>Hearing unaccepted pronouns now gradually increases tolerance unless those pronouns are actively rejected.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>SSS footwork now removes forest and moor hobbling</strong>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Improved fox and rabbit transformation traits</strong>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Thrill of the Chase</strong> can be restored in the mirror after a Fox Genome Dump.</li>
					<li><strong>Strong Feet</strong> now grants its intended Dancing and Athletics bonuses, both shown under Characteristics.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Improved the Virtual Pet minigame interface</strong>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Fixed museum Journal and antique collection errors</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Unsupported antique entries in older or modded saves no longer break museum displays or affect collection progress.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed clothing filters and missing trait tooltips</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Shop filters no longer fail on blindfolds.</li>
					<li>Added missing blindfold and shackle trait descriptions in shops and wardrobes.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed Water Dragon routes and egg-laying</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>The coastal route to the hidden beach now appears as soon as eggs are ready, without needing to sleep.</li>
					<li>Fixed nest options for fertilised clutches and supported anal egg-laying, while preserving nest progress, lab restrictions, and overdue penalties.</li>
					<li>Later egg-laying trips no longer replay the first nest discovery.</li>
					<li>Returning to the Water Dragon lab now preserves <strong>Hard mode</strong> and no longer says it was disabled.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Preserved partner pregnancy outcomes for Water Dragons</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Babies fathered by <strong>Black Wolf, Great Hawk, Alex, Poppy, or Ivory Wraith</strong> now use their normal birth and child-content routes rather than going to the Water Dragon nest.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed pet encounter names</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Pet attacks now refer to named NPCs by their names rather than their titles.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed character sprite layering and animation cleanup</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Arm skin and shoulder tattoos no longer render over jackets or shirts, including raised-arm poses.</li>
					<li>Fixed duplicate character layers after changing passages and animations continuing after images were disabled.</li>
					<li>Fixed pregnancy/vision clothing crossover: Hopeless Cycle and other painting/vision scenes now remove the player's coat, overskirt, scarf, and bag from the vision character and restore them afterwards.</li>
					<li>Fixed two-tone modded hair dyes so the second colour aligns correctly on all hairstyles, in and out of combat.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed corrupted startup variables</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Semen stats now initialise before startup clamping; bank payment dates wait until the game clock is ready.</li>
					<li>Added safeguards against clothing triggering corrupted-variable errors.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed Ear Slime and parasite issues</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Fixed a quotation-mark error in the café's <strong>Cafe Eat</strong> scene.</li>
					<li>Silenced Ear Slimes no longer reward or ruin orgasms, and ruined-orgasm effects no longer carry into later encounters.</li>
					<li>Removing Ear Slimes now removes their dependent parasites across all X-Change bodies and repairs leftovers in affected saves.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fix NPCs repeatedly grabbing an already-lifted short skirt</strong>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed Colosseum sex and aftermath errors</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Restored oral actions missing in some saves.</li>
					<li>Fixed endless <strong>Next</strong> loops and unfair bans when Breeder effects or X-Change Purity prevent the player from finishing.</li>
					<li>Refusing a match-fixing bribe no longer skips the breeding aftermath; fixer follow-up and match-state cleanup now work correctly.</li>
					<li>Fixed missing NPC warnings in brothel pregnancy encounters and misleading aftermath text.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed pursuer chastity punishments after escape</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Pursuers no longer fit chastity devices or steal keys after the player has escaped.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed disappearing and stuck clothing</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Backpacks no longer remain equipped when changing into default Swimwear.</li>
					<li>Fixed jackets showing as <strong>naked</strong> in removal menus.</li>
					<li>Fixed the park underwear-running blackmail task checking the wrong clothing state.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed Avery's date progression</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Permanently pilled players no longer get stuck during Avery's date.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed NPC positioning and beast oral interactions</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>NPCs pinned during sex now render at the correct position.</li>
					<li>Beasts such as Great Hawk and Black Wolf no longer randomly withdraw during oral every turn; they remain until the interaction actually ends.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Fixed farm and other scene interactions</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Resisting Harper's livestock examination now uses its own Strength check.</li>
					<li>Beach Phallus Project acceptance now opens the changing-room scene.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon images" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</span> Art and Graphics</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Added new hairstyles</strong>
				<ul>
					<li>Vanilla hair sides: <strong>Blunt Twintails</strong> and <strong>Outward-flicked</strong>; fringes: <strong>Rounded</strong>, <strong>Layered Sweep</strong>, and <strong>Outward-flicked</strong>, by <strong>kon (konpm)</strong>.</li>
					<li>Added the matching <strong>GooseFem</strong> versions by <strong>Leni (lenlenienii)</strong>.</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Added Vanilla Modded Faces 14–19</strong> by <strong>Snowy</strong>.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Added Mysterious breast tape</strong> by <strong>Flo</strong>.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Cleaned up the Mysterious image pack</strong>.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
